% The Pythagorean theorem: in a right-angled triangle, the square on the
% longest side equals the sum of the squares on the other two. The program
% sorts triangles by comparing those squares, finds whole-number hypotenuses,
% and generates the primitive Pythagorean triples with Euclid's formula.
% 3-4-5, 5-12-13 and 6-8-10 are right-angled, 4-5-6 is acute, 2-3-4 obtuse,
% and 1-2-3 is no triangle at all. Legs 20 and 21 have hypotenuse 29, legs 1
% and 1 none in whole numbers. Seven primitive triples have a hypotenuse of at
% most 50, from 3-4-5 to 9-40-41.
% Shows comparisons of computed squares, a square root checked against whole
% numbers, values generated from lists, Euclid's algorithm for coprime numbers
% and a count over the generated triples.
% After Euclid's Elements, Book I, Proposition 47, and Book X, Lemma 1 to
% Proposition 29.

the templates are:
    *a triangle* has sides *a number* and *a number* and longest side *a number*,
    *a triangle* is no triangle,
    *a triangle* is right-angled,
    *a triangle* is acute,
    *a triangle* is obtuse,
    legs *a number* and *a number* are given,
    legs *a number* and *a number* have hypotenuse *a number*,
    legs *a number* and *a number* have no whole hypotenuse,
    the greatest common divisor of *a number* and *a number* is *a number*,
    *a number* and *a number* and *a number* is a primitive Pythagorean triple,
    *a number* primitive triples have a hypotenuse of at most *a number*.

the knowledge base pythagoras includes:

% Three lengths make a triangle only when the two shorter add up to more than
% the longest.
a triangle is no triangle
    if the triangle has sides a number A and a number B and longest side a number C
    and A + B =< C.

% Book I, Proposition 47 and its converse, Proposition 48: the angle opposite
% the longest side is right exactly when its square is the sum of the others.
a triangle is right-angled
    if the triangle has sides a number A and a number B and longest side a number C
    and A + B > C
    and A * A + B * B = C * C.

a triangle is acute
    if the triangle has sides a number A and a number B and longest side a number C
    and A + B > C
    and A * A + B * B > C * C.

a triangle is obtuse
    if the triangle has sides a number A and a number B and longest side a number C
    and A + B > C
    and A * A + B * B < C * C.

% A hypotenuse is whole when the root of the sum of squares, rounded, squares
% back to that sum.
legs a number A and a number B have hypotenuse a number C
    if legs A and B are given
    and S = A * A + B * B
    and C = round(sqrt(S))
    and C * C = S.

legs a number A and a number B have no whole hypotenuse
    if legs A and B are given
    and it is not the case that
        legs A and B have hypotenuse a number C.

the greatest common divisor of a number A and 0 is A
    if A > 0.

the greatest common divisor of a number A and a number B is a number G
    if B > 0
    and R = A mod B
    and the greatest common divisor of B and R is G.

% Euclid's formula: for coprime M > N of opposite parity, M*M - N*N, 2*M*N
% and M*M + N*N give a primitive triple. Report the shorter leg first.
a number A and a number B and a number C is a primitive Pythagorean triple
    if a number M is in [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
    and a number N is in [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
    and M > N
    and (M - N) mod 2 = 1
    and the greatest common divisor of M and N is 1
    and X = M * M - N * N
    and Y = 2 * M * N
    and C = M * M + N * N
    and the minimum of X and Y is A
    and the maximum of X and Y is B.

a number K primitive triples have a hypotenuse of at most a number L
    if L is in [25, 50]
    and K is the count of each C such that
        a number A and a number B and C is a primitive Pythagorean triple
        and C =< L.

scenario geometry is:
    t1 has sides 3 and 4 and longest side 5.
    t2 has sides 5 and 12 and longest side 13.
    t3 has sides 6 and 8 and longest side 10.
    t4 has sides 4 and 5 and longest side 6.
    t5 has sides 2 and 3 and longest side 4.
    t6 has sides 1 and 2 and longest side 3.
    legs 20 and 21 are given.
    legs 9 and 40 are given.
    legs 1 and 1 are given.
    legs 2 and 3 are given.
    right expects answers ["t1 is right-angled", "t2 is right-angled", "t3 is right-angled"].
    acute expects answers ["t4 is acute"].
    obtuse expects answers ["t5 is obtuse"].
    degenerate expects answers ["t6 is no triangle"].
    hypotenuses expects answers ["legs 20 and 21 have hypotenuse 29", "legs 9 and 40 have hypotenuse 41"].
    irrational expects answers ["legs 1 and 1 have no whole hypotenuse", "legs 2 and 3 have no whole hypotenuse"].
    triples expects answers ["3 and 4 and 5 is a primitive Pythagorean triple",
        "5 and 12 and 13 is a primitive Pythagorean triple", "8 and 15 and 17 is a primitive Pythagorean triple",
        "7 and 24 and 25 is a primitive Pythagorean triple", "20 and 21 and 29 is a primitive Pythagorean triple",
        "9 and 40 and 41 is a primitive Pythagorean triple", "12 and 35 and 37 is a primitive Pythagorean triple",
        "11 and 60 and 61 is a primitive Pythagorean triple", "28 and 45 and 53 is a primitive Pythagorean triple",
        "33 and 56 and 65 is a primitive Pythagorean triple", "13 and 84 and 85 is a primitive Pythagorean triple"].
    counts expects answers ["4 primitive triples have a hypotenuse of at most 25",
        "7 primitive triples have a hypotenuse of at most 50"].

query right is:
    which triangle is right-angled.

query acute is:
    which triangle is acute.

query obtuse is:
    which triangle is obtuse.

query degenerate is:
    which triangle is no triangle.

query hypotenuses is:
    legs which number and which other number have hypotenuse which hypotenuse.

query irrational is:
    legs which number and which other number have no whole hypotenuse.

query triples is:
    which number and which second number and which third number is a primitive Pythagorean triple.

query counts is:
    which count primitive triples have a hypotenuse of at most which limit.
